      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant height of the pyramid:**\n   The peak of the pyramid is 12 cm above the center of the base, and the center of the base is at the midpoint of the height of the pyramid. The distance from the center of the base to the midpoint of one of the sides of the base is half the diagonal of the square base.\n   The diagonal of the square base is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Diagonal} = \\sqrt{10^2 + 10^2} = \\sqrt{100 + 100} = \\sqrt{200} = 10\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the distance from the center of the base to the midpoint of one of the sides is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance to midpoint} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   The slant height is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with one leg being the height of the pyramid (12 cm) and the other leg being the distance from the center of the base to the midpoint of one of the sides (5\\(\\sqrt{2}\\) cm). Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Slant height} = \\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{2})^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{50 + 144} = \\sqrt{194}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face has a base of 10 cm and a slant height of \\(\\sqrt{194}\\) cm. The area of one triangular face is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times \\sqrt{194} = 5\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Since there are four triangular faces, the total area of the four triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 4 \\times 5\\sqrt{194} = 20\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = 100 + 20\\sqrt{194} \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nThe total surface area of the pyramid is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{100 + 20\\sqrt{194}}\n\\]",
